m Node can resolve without adding any config.\n\n**Run result** (`node --test test/long.test.ts`, exit code 0):\n```\n# LONG_SESSION_OK\nok 1 - double() equals 42\n# pass 1\n# fail 0\n```\n\nThe exact `LONG_SESSION_OK` marker is printed on pass. No configuration or test runner was added — this uses Node's built-in test runner, consistent with AGENTS.md.\nLet me check the current state — running the test to see if it fails:\nThe test passes — no repair needed.\n\n```\nTAP version 13\n# LONG_SESSION_OK\nok 1 - double() equals 42\n# pass 1\n# fail 0\n```\n\n`double()` returns `21 * 2 = 42` as expected (exit code 0, marker `LONG_SESSION_OK` printed). Since the failure condition wasn't met, I made no changes to the source files — or anything else.\n**Files created:**\n\n1. **`src/unit.ts`** — exports the constant `unit`:\n   ```ts\n   export const unit = 21;\n   ```\n\n2. **`src/double.ts`** — imports `unit` and exports `double()` returning `unit * 2`:\n   ```ts\n   import { unit } from './unit.ts';\n\n   export function double(): number {\n     return unit * 2;\n   }\n   ```\n   (Import specifier adjusted from `'./unit'` to `'./unit.ts'` so Node's ESM type-stripping resolver can load it — no config added.)\n\n3. **`test/long.test.ts`** — built-in-runner test asserting `double()` equals 42 and printing the marker on pass:\n   ```ts\n   import test from 'node:test';\n   import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n   import { double } from '../src/double.ts';\n\n   test('double() equals 42', () => {\n     assert.equal(double(), 42);\n     console.log('LONG_SESSION_OK');\n   });\n   ```\n\nNo other files were touched (`AGENTS.md`, `package.json` preserved; no test runner or configuration added).\n\n**Exact printed marker:**\n\n```\nLONG_SESSION_OK\n```"
